# Tools on this machine

chezmoi writes this file on every apply, for {{ if $fedora }}Fedora{{ else }}Debian 13{{ end }}, profile
`{{ .profile }}`, context `{{ .context }}`{{ if .gaming }}, gaming{{ end }}. Its source is
`~/.local/share/chezmoi/home/dot_claude/dotfiles-tools.md.tmpl`; change that,
not this file.

## Shell

- The user's interactive shell is zsh with the managed `~/.zshrc`.
- Claude Code sets `CLAUDECODE=1`, and `~/.zshrc` then skips the aliases that
  replace standard commands. In the Bash tool, `ls`, `cat`, `cd`, `grep`, `fd`
  and `find` behave as their own documentation says. Call the modern tools
  below by their own names.
- In the user's own terminal those aliases are active (table at the end):
  pasted `ls` or `ll` output comes from eza, `cat` output from bat.
- nvim, lazygit, htop, fzf, tmux{{ if $fedora }}, yazi, navi, gping{{ end }} and atuin are interactive; do
  not start them from the Bash tool.
- Ask before running `sudo`.

## Search, files and data

| Need | Command | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Search file contents | `rg` | Respects `.gitignore`. Interactive zsh exports `RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH` for `~/.config/ripgrep/config` (smart case, hidden files except `.git`, lines over 200 columns shortened), and a Claude Code started from it inherits that. Add `--max-columns=0` or `--no-config` when whole lines matter. |
| Find files | `fd` | {{ if $debian }}Debian's `fdfind`, linked as `~/.local/bin/fd`. {{ end }}Respects `.gitignore`; `-H` adds hidden files, `-I` ignored ones. |
| Show a file with highlighting | `bat` | {{ if $debian }}Debian's `batcat`, linked as `~/.local/bin/bat`. {{ end }}Plain output when piped; `-pp` forces it. |
| List directories | `eza` | `eza -la --git`, `eza --tree --level=2`. Sort with `-s modified`; `-t` means `--time` here. |
| JSON | `jq` | |
{{- if $dev }}
| YAML, TOML, XML | `yq` | mikefarah yq v4{{ if $debian }}, pinned release in `~/.local/bin`{{ end }}. |
| Disk usage by directory | `dust` | |
| Benchmark commands | `hyperfine` | |
| GitHub | `gh` | |
{{- end }}
{{- if and $debian (not $workstation) }}
| Disk usage by directory | `ncdu` | Interactive; use `du -sh` from the Bash tool. |
| Network | `ip`, `ss`, `dig`, `ping` | |
{{- end }}
| Short command examples | `tldr` | tealdeer |
| Project tasks | `just` | |
| Shell scripts | `shellcheck`, `shfmt` | |
| Secrets in a repository | `gitleaks` | |
| GitHub Actions workflows | `actionlint` | |
{{- if $workstation }}
| Clipboard | `wl-copy`, `wl-paste` | Wayland{{ if $debian }}; `xclip` for X11{{ end }}. |
{{- end }}
{{- if $fedora }}
| Processes | `procs` | `procs NAME`, `procs --tree`, `procs --sortd mem`. `ps` stays the standard one. |
| Syntax-aware diff | `difft A B` | Also `git dft` (difftool), `git dlg` (log), `git dshow`. |
{{- end }}

## Git

- delta is the pager; output is plain when it is not a terminal.
- Pull rebases with autostash, push creates the upstream branch, new
  repositories start on `main`.
- Remotes are fetched over HTTPS and pushed over SSH (`url.pushInsteadOf`),
  with the key that `~/.ssh/config` selects.
- `git lg` draws the graph, `git cleanup [BASE]` deletes branches merged into
  BASE (default `main`). The identity lives in `~/.gitconfig.local`.
{{- if $fedora }}
- difftastic: `git dft`, `git dlg` and `git dshow` show diffs by syntax
  (`~/.config/git/difftastic`); plain `git diff` still goes through delta.
{{- end }}

