## Packages and dotfiles
{{ if $fedora }}
- dnf installs packages, with COPR for Starship, LazyGit, Klassy and Bibata
  cursors and Microsoft's repository for VS Code. Pinned GitHub releases add yazi and ya, gping
  (`~/.local/bin`) and fzf-tab (`~/.local/share/zsh/plugins`).
{{- else }}
- apt installs packages from the official Debian 13 repositories only. Pinned
  GitHub releases add what Debian lacks: chezmoi, nvim{{ if $workstation }}, uv, uvx, yq{{ end }} and
  actionlint.
{{- end }}
- To add a tool for good, add it to
  `~/.local/share/chezmoi/home/.chezmoidata/packages.yaml` and run
  `chezmoi apply`; the package script installs only what is missing and uses
  sudo.
- chezmoi manages the dotfiles. Edit the sources in
  `~/.local/share/chezmoi/home` (`.tmpl` files are templates), check with
  `chezmoi diff`, deploy with `chezmoi apply`. `scripts/verify.sh` in that
  checkout checks the machine.
- Settings for this machine only go in the local files, which chezmoi leaves
  alone: `~/.zshrc.settings`, `~/.zshrc.local`, `~/.zshenv.local`,
  `~/.gitconfig.local`, `~/.ssh/config.local`, `~/.tmux.conf.local` and
  `~/.config/kitty/kitty.d/*.conf`.

## Aliases in the user's terminal

| Typed | Runs |
|---|---|
| `ls`, `ll`, `la` | eza with icons and directories first; `ll` and `la` add a header, Git status and ISO dates |
| `tree`, `lt`, `ltt` | `eza --tree`, at any depth, two or three levels |
| `cat` | `bat --paging=never --style=plain` |
| `cd` | zoxide's `z` |
| `vi`, `vim` | `nvim` |
| `top` | `htop` |
| `fd` | `fd --hidden --exclude .git` |
| `grep`, `diff`, `ip` | the same command with colour |
| `df`, `du`, `free` | human-readable sizes |
| `g`, `gs`, `gd`, `gl`, `gco`, … | Git shortcuts |
| `lg`, `ai`, `air` | LazyGit; Claude; Claude resuming a session |
{{- if $fedora }}
| `y` | yazi; quitting with `q` moves the shell to yazi's last directory |
| `s`, `icat`, `kd` | Inside Kitty only: `kitten ssh`, `kitten icat`, `kitten diff` |
| `Ctrl+G` | navi cheat sheets (`~/.local/share/navi/cheats/dotfiles`) |
| `Tab` | fzf-tab: completion in fzf with previews; `<` and `>` switch groups |
{{- end }}
{{- if $fedora }}
| `dnfup`, `dnfi`, `dnfs`, `dnfrm`, `dnfinfo` | dnf upgrade, install, search, remove, info |
{{- else }}
| `aptup`, `apti`, `apts`, `aptrm`, `aptshow` | apt upgrade, install, search, remove, show |
{{- end }}

`DOTFILES_ENABLE_COMMAND_OVERRIDES=1` in `~/.zshrc.settings` also maps `less`
to bat, `grep` to rg, `find` to fd and `mkdir` to `mkdir -p`. Shell helpers:
`fe`, `fcd`, `frg`, `fga`, `fh`, `fkill`, `groot`, `gclone`, `gwip`, `gunwip`,
`mkcd`, `extract`, `serve`, `psg`, `activate`, `tm`. All of them are described
in `~/.local/share/chezmoi/docs/ALIASES.md`.
